  "discussion": "Surf along north and west-facing shores will dip briefly from warning levels to advisory levels today as a large, long-period north- northwest swell fades. However, a new extra-large, long-period north- northwest swell is expected to arrive this evening into tonight and peak overnight into Thursday. This will bring even larger warning level surf to north and west-facing shores possibly into Friday. The swell will gradually fade through the weekend. Surf heights along east-facing shores will be somewhat elevated through Friday due to wrapping from the north-northwest swell, but are expected to remain below advisory levels. Surf along south-facing shores will remain tiny to small through the next few days.",
